1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,620
This is the scoreboard.

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:03,500
It sleeps,

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,899
but the e-paper still shows the last game.

4
00:00:07,753 --> 00:00:11,381
Press any key, or bump the table, and it wakes.

5
00:00:12,373 --> 00:00:13,973
Tap your badge on the right.

6
00:00:13,973 --> 00:00:14,733
Bip.

7
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:15,493
Bidi-ding.

8
00:00:15,493 --> 00:00:16,373
Bob's in,

9
00:00:16,373 --> 00:00:19,302
and the badge target glows in his colour.

10
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:22,012
All in?

11
00:00:22,012 --> 00:00:23,692
Pick your teams, draw them at random,

12
00:00:23,692 --> 00:00:25,852
or let MMR make them fair.

13
00:00:25,852 --> 00:00:26,812
Wrong ends?

14
00:00:26,812 --> 00:00:28,595
Swap sides.

15
00:00:29,245 --> 00:00:30,365
Then just play.

16
00:00:30,365 --> 00:00:33,684
Goals turn up by themselves, with a little ding.

17
00:00:33,684 --> 00:00:34,404
Who scored?

18
00:00:34,404 --> 00:00:36,004
Press a name, or don't.

19
00:00:36,004 --> 00:00:37,204
Carol, apparently.

20
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:38,757
Own goal.

21
00:00:38,807 --> 00:00:39,607
Not a goal?

22
00:00:39,607 --> 00:00:43,582
Undo asks first, then plays the ding backwards.

23
00:00:45,632 --> 00:00:47,712
The winning goal gets a little celebration.

24
00:00:47,712 --> 00:00:51,472
Ten seconds to undo, then it's in MMR.

25
00:00:51,472 --> 00:00:52,832
Same four again?

26
00:00:52,832 --> 00:00:54,375
Rematch.

27
00:00:56,832 --> 00:00:59,472
An unknown badge gets a QR code.

28
00:00:59,472 --> 00:01:00,592
Scan it yourself,

29
00:01:00,592 --> 00:01:02,512
or let a colleague do it for you.

30
00:01:02,512 --> 00:01:05,191
Link the badge, and you're in.

31
00:01:06,341 --> 00:01:08,661
Volume lives in the admin settings:

32
00:01:08,661 --> 00:01:10,741
Off, Low, Medium, High.

33
00:01:10,741 --> 00:01:12,421
No secret key combo.

34
00:01:12,421 --> 00:01:14,358
We know our colleagues.

35
00:01:15,508 --> 00:01:17,108
Three AA batteries,

36
00:01:17,108 --> 00:01:19,428
about two and a half to three months a set,

37
00:01:19,428 --> 00:01:20,548
by our estimate.

38
00:01:20,548 --> 00:01:23,312
When they're flat, it says so.

39
00:01:23,662 --> 00:01:26,687
It keeps score, so you don't have to.
